{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The rider has met the initial burden under POL-RD-08: the trip_record (EV-TRIP-00109), gps_trace (EV-GPS-00109) and fare_breakdown (EV-FARE-00109) all describe the same trip TRP-00109 with a consistent start at 18:21:10, and the unimpaired gps_trace (coverage 100%, no gaps, weight 1.0) records a trace_distance_km of 13.76 against the booked optimal_distance_km of 6.4, an excess of 7.36 km or 115%, which exceeds both the 0.8 km and 20% establishment thresholds in POL-RD-01.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00109", "EV-GPS-00109", "EV-FARE-00109"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver has discharged the shifted burden under POL-RD-08 by pointing to the chat_log (EV-CHAT-00109) and POL-RD-04: the rider's own message MSG-00109-001, sent at 18:22:06 (56 seconds after the trip started at 18:21:10), asked 'hi can stop at jurong point first? need to grab something 5 min' and carries a waypoint_hint resolving to VEN-JURONG-POINT, so the instruction comes from the rider, is timestamped before the vehicle left the optimal corridor (or within 3 minutes after) and identifies the place specifically enough to act on. The gps_trace (EV-GPS-00109) corroborates it: the vehicle was stationary 38 m from the Jurong Point PHV pickup point for 366 seconds, within the 200 m test POL-RD-04 requires.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00109", "EV-GPS-00109"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Under POL-RD-04 the deviation is exonerated to the extent it is attributable to that rider-requested detour, and the excess distance between leaving and rejoining the optimal corridor is excluded before POL-RD-01 and POL-RD-02 are applied. The whole 7.36 km excess is the detour via Jurong Point: the trip ran from the Clementi MRT pickup to the Bukit Batok MRT dropoff via the requested stop, and no other off-corridor driving is shown. After the exclusion the remaining excess is nil, so the POL-RD-01 establishment test fails; no deviation exists and, under POL-RD-01, the outcome is NO_ACTION however the rider characterises the trip. The rider's own request caused the longer route and the 34-minute duration, so the rider cannot recover the contested SGD 12.00.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00109", "EV-TRIP-00109", "EV-CHAT-00109"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider was under-billed, not over-billed. The fare_breakdown (EV-FARE-00109) shows distance_charged_km of 9.60 while the gps_trace (EV-GPS-00109) records 13.76 km, a shortfall of 4.16 km that exceeds the 1.0 km threshold in POL-RD-04; the metered total of SGD 21.32 is therefore less than the SGD 24.44 that would correspond to the full trace distance. Under POL-RD-04 the driver may be granted DRIVER_COMPENSATION of SGD 3.15 (4.16 km x SGD 0.75, rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05, capped at SGD 15.00), and under POL-GEN-03 the rider's own charge stands; the rider is not carrying an overcharge and is not entitled to a refund of the contested amount.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00109", "EV-GPS-00109"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.trace_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No other clause gives the rider a remedy. The traffic advisory artifact EV-ADVIS-00109-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT), so no road-closure exoneration under POL-RD-03 is available and the detour is not explained by any road condition. The trip_record (EV-TRIP-00109) shows no pickup or dropoff amendment (pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are null), so POL-RD-05 does not apply. The fare_breakdown (EV-FARE-00109) shows fare_model METERED and quoted_fare_sgd null, so POL-RD-11 does not apply. The vehicle_type is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12 does not apply. The driver_profile (EV-DPROF-00109) shows deviation_flags_90d of 0 and completed_trips_90d of 511, so no repeat-deviation pattern is established under POL-RD-06 and the material finding does not license a full refund.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00109-01", "EV-TRIP-00109", "EV-FARE-00109", "EV-DPROF-00109"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-05", "POL-RD-11", "POL-RD-12", "POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no pass-through or billing-integrity correction for the rider: the fare_breakdown (EV-FARE-00109) shows erp_gantries empty and airport_surcharge 0.0, so no off-route ERP, toll or phantom gantry line exists to refund under POL-RD-09, and no surcharge was applied. The rider's contested amount therefore cannot be recovered on any billing-integrity ground.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00109"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

[
  {
    "text": "The rider has met the initial burden under POL-RD-08: the trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown all carry trip_id TRP-00109 and consistent timestamps (the trip started at 2026-07-21T18:21:10+08:00, the GPS trace's first fix is at the same moment, and the fare was charged after the trip ended), and the gps_trace is unimpaired (100% coverage, no gaps, weight 1.0). Its derived deviation figures show a trace_distance_km of 13.76 against an optimal_distance_km of 6.4, an excess of 7.36 km or 115%, which passes both POL-RD-01 establishment tests (excess greater than 20% of optimal and greater than 0.8 km absolute) and is a MATERIAL deviation because the excess exceeds 50% of optimal.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00109", "EV-GPS-00109", "EV-FARE-00109"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-08"],
    "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  },
  {
    "text": "The rider's own chat message MSG-00109-001, sent at 18:22:06 (within three minutes of the vehicle leaving the optimal corridor), asked to 'stop at Jurong Point first' and carries waypoint_hint VEN-JURONG-POINT; the gps_trace corroborates it by placing the vehicle stationary 38 m from that waypoint for 366 seconds. Under POL-RD-04 the deviation is EXONERATED to the extent it is attributable to that rider instruction, and the excess distance between leaving and rejoining the optimal corridor is excluded before POL-RD-01 and POL-RD-02 are applied. Because the entire 7.36 km excess is the detour to and from the rider-requested Jurong Point stop, no deviation remains after the exclusion, so the rider's claim for a distance-based refund is not sustained and the outcome on the rider's claim is NO_ACTION, which under POL-GEN-03 leaves the charge in place because the rider filed the dispute.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00109", "EV-GPS-00109"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-GEN-03"],
    "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  },
  {
    "text": "The rider's complaint that the SGD 21.32 fare is unreasonable is not supported: the fare_breakdown records distance_charged_km of 9.60, which is less than both the gps_trace's 13.76 km and the trip_record's actual_distance_km of 13.8, so the rider was under-billed for distance rather than overcharged. There are no ERP or toll lines (erp_gantries is empty, tolls_erp is 0.00) and no airport surcharge, so no charge line lacks a counterpart in the trace and no billing-integrity refund arises under POL-RD-09(4). The shortfall is 4.16 unbilled kilometres, which under the POL-RD-04 compensation limb pays SGD 3.15 to the driver, not a refund to the rider, as POL-GEN-03 provides.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00109", "EV-GPS-00109", "EV-TRIP-00109"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-09", "POL-GEN-03"],
    "relies_on": "derived.deviation.trace_distance_km",
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  },
  {
    "text": "Because the pre-exclusion excess is MATERIAL, POL-RD-06 requires the driver_profile check. The driver_profile shows deviation_flags_90d of 0 and completed_trips_90d of 511, so no repeat-deviation pattern is established (0 is fewer than 3, and 0 divided by 511 is far below 0.05). POL-RD-06 therefore does not license a FULL_REFUND uplift or a driver-conduct referral on pattern grounds, and the rider's request that the driver be banned is not supported by this trip's evidence.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00109"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06"],
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  }
]

[
  {
    "text": "The detour was requested by the rider herself: MSG-00109-001 in the chat log is sent by the RIDER at 18:22:06 and reads 'hi can stop at jurong point first? need to grab something 5 min', and it carries a waypoint_hint identifying Jurong Point, PHV Pickup Point, venue_id VEN-JURONG-POINT. That is a rider instruction identifying a place specifically enough to act on, satisfying POL-RD-04(a) and (c).",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00109"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  },
  {
    "text": "The instruction was timestamped within the window POL-RD-04(b) allows: the trip started at 18:21:10 (EV-TRIP-00109) and the rider's request was sent at 18:22:06, only 56 seconds later, and the driver accepted at 18:22:31. The request was therefore made before the vehicle left the optimal corridor for the detour, and in any event well within 3 minutes of the start.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00109", "EV-CHAT-00109"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  },
  {
    "text": "The GPS trace corroborates the requested stop: EV-GPS-00109 is COMPLETE at weight 1.0 and its admissibility note records that the vehicle was stationary 38 m from the Jurong Point PHV pickup point recorded as the waypoint_hint on MSG-00109-001, for 366 seconds. That is within the 200 m proximity POL-RD-04 requires, and the 366-second stationary period matches the driver's account of waiting about six minutes.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00109", "EV-CHAT-00109"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  },
  {
    "text": "Because the detour is attributable to the rider's own instruction, POL-RD-04 exonerates it and excludes the excess distance between leaving and rejoining the optimal corridor before POL-RD-01 and POL-RD-02 are applied. The only reason the vehicle left the booked optimal route (Clementi Rd -> Bukit Batok East Ave 3, optimal_distance_km 6.4) was the Jurong Point stop; the measured excess of 7.36 km (trace_distance_km 13.76 less optimal 6.4) is entirely that detour, so after exclusion no excess remains.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00109", "EV-TRIP-00109", "EV-CHAT-00109"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-01"],
    "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  },
  {
    "text": "With the rider-requested detour excluded, the remaining excess is zero, so POL-RD-01's establishment tests (excess >20% of optimal and >0.8 km) fail and no deviation exists. The rider's characterisation of the trip as an unjustified 14 km detour is therefore not supported: the outcome on her claim is that the charge stands, and no refund under POL-RD-02 is available.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00109", "EV-TRIP-00109", "EV-CHAT-00109"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-04"],
    "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  },
  {
    "text": "The derived deviation block flags the unadjusted excess as 'material' (excess_pct 115.00, above the 50% material threshold in POL-RD-01), but POL-RD-01 expressly requires materiality to be assessed on the excess REMAINING after any POL-RD-04 adjustment, not on the excess as first measured. After the Jurong Point detour is excluded, the remaining excess is zero, so the deviation is not material and the POL-RD-06 driver_profile check is not triggered by a material deviation.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00109", "EV-TRIP-00109", "EV-CHAT-00109"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-04"],
    "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  },
  {
    "text": "Even if the tribunal looked at the unadjusted figures, POL-RD-06 establishes no repeat-deviation pattern: the citable field driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 (the lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter is not the field this clause names and is not relied on), and driver_profile.completed_trips_90d is 511, so the ratio is 0.00, far below the 0.05 threshold and the 3-flag trigger. No pattern is established, so no FULL_REFUND uplift and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral follows.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00109"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  },
  {
    "text": "The rider carries the initial burden under POL-RD-08, but the driver has discharged the shifted burden by citing EV-CHAT-00109 and POL-RD-04. The citable rider_profile field deviation_claims_60d is 1, below the 4-claim trigger in POL-RD-08, so the clause's extra corroboration requirement does not apply; no other rider profile field is relied on.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-00109", "EV-CHAT-00109", "EV-GPS-00109"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-GEN-01"],
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  },
  {
    "text": "The fare breakdown billed the rider for only 9.6 km (distance_charged_km) while the GPS trace records 13.76 km (derived.deviation.trace_distance_km), a shortfall of 4.16 km, which exceeds the 1.0 km threshold in POL-RD-04. The driver is therefore entitled to DRIVER_COMPENSATION at SGD 0.75 per unbilled kilometre: 4.16 x 0.75 = 3.12, rounded UP to the nearest SGD 0.05 = SGD 3.15, within the SGD 15.00 cap. The policy's own note to POL-RD-04 gives this exact case: 4.16 unbilled kilometres pays SGD 3.15, not 3.12.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00109", "EV-GPS-00109"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
    "relies_on": "derived.deviation.trace_distance_km",
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  },
  {
    "text": "The rider filed this dispute and the fare stands charged: fare_breakdown.payment_status is CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd is 0.00. Because the detour is exonerated, the rider's refund claim is not supported and her charge of SGD 21.32 stands; because the driver was underbilled, he is owed SGD 3.15. Under POL-GEN-03 the ruling value is DRIVER_COMPENSATION, amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd are both SGD 3.15, and the filing party's own charge is left in place.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00109", "EV-GPS-00109"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-RD-04"],
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  },
  {
    "text": "No traffic advisory covers this trip: EV-ADVIS-00109-01 is MISSING, with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, and its own note states the detour is explained by the rider's own instruction, not by any road condition. Under POL-GEN-02 a missing artifact can carry no fact, so POL-RD-03 is unavailable; the driver does not need it, because POL-RD-04 already exonerates the detour.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00109-01"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-GEN-02"],
    "asserted_weight": 0.0
  },
  {
    "text": "POL-RD-05 does not apply: the trip record shows no pickup or dropoff amendment (pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are null, amended_optimal_distance_km is null), and the trip record's own note states this is POL-RD-04 territory, not POL-RD-05. POL-RD-12 also does not apply: trip_record.vehicle_type is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, and solo_optimal_distance_km is null.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00109"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-05", "POL-RD-12"],
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  },
  {
    "text": "POL-RD-11 does not apply: fare_breakdown.fare_model is METERED, not UPFRONT_QUOTE, and quoted_fare_sgd is null. The rider therefore cannot invoke the upfront-quote route, and because the deviation is exonerated under POL-RD-04, POL-RD-02 does not run and no distance-or-time refund is available to her.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00109"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11", "POL-RD-04"],
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  },
  {
    "text": "No ERP or toll refund is due. The detour was rider-caused under POL-RD-04, so POL-RD-09(3) provides that no ERP refund is due; in any event the fare carries no ERP or toll lines (erp_gantries is empty, tolls_erp is 0.00) and no airport surcharge (airport_surcharge 0.00, and the pickup is Clementi MRT, not an airport), so there is no pass-through correction under POL-RD-09.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00109", "EV-TRIP-00109"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-04"],
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  },
  {
    "text": "The GPS trace is unimpaired for policy purposes: EV-GPS-00109 has 100% coverage, no gaps (max_gap_sec 0.0), a 10-second sampling interval, and admissibility weight 1.0, so it does not meet POL-RD-07(a) to (c). The deciding facts it carries (trace_distance_km 13.76 and excess_km 7.36) are therefore carried by an artifact at weight 1.0, and under POL-GEN-02 the confidence cap is 1.0, well above the 0.70 escalation floor; no escalation under POL-RD-10(1) is engaged.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00109"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-GEN-02"],
    "relies_on": "derived.deviation.trace_distance_km",
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  },
  {
    "text": "The rider's allegation that the driver 'anyhow drive to increase the fare' is contradicted by the fare breakdown: the driver was billed for only 9.6 km while the trace records 13.76 km, so the driver did not charge for the full distance driven and in fact was underbilled. The driver's own statement on file notes the receipt shows 9.6 km, and the fare artifact confirms distance_charged_km is 9.6.",
    "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00109", "EV-GPS-00109"],
    "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
    "relies_on": "derived.deviation.trace_distance_km",
    "asserted_weight": 1.0
  }
]

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 3.15,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 3.15,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 1.0,
    "explanation": "To the rider: You asked for a refund of the SGD 21.32 fare, saying the driver took an unjustified detour to Jurong Point. The chat log (EV-CHAT-00109) shows you messaged at 18:22:06 asking to 'stop at Jurong Point first', and the GPS trace (EV-GPS-00109) confirms the car stopped within 38 m of that pickup point for about six minutes. Because the detour was your own request, POL-RD-04 excludes that distance. After the exclusion, no excess distance remains, so no route deviation is established under POL-RD-01 and no fare refund is due to you. Your refund claim is not supported and the SGD 21.32 charge stands. In fact, the fare records show you were billed for less distance than was driven, so the allegation that the driver inflated the fare is not supported.\n\nTo the driver: The fare breakdown (EV-FARE-00109) billed only 9.6 km, but the GPS trace shows you drove 13.76 km. The shortfall is 4.16 km, which exceeds the 1.0 km threshold in POL-RD-04. You are therefore granted driver compensation of SGD 3.15 (4.16 km x SGD 0.75 = SGD 3.12, rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05). This is paid to you and does not change the rider's charge.\n\nThe missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-00109-01) is irrelevant because the detour is explained by your chat request, not by road conditions. The driver's profile shows no repeat-deviation pattern (deviation_flags_90d is 0), so no conduct referral is made. All evidence relied on is complete and unimpaired (weight 1.0), so confidence is 1.0. No referrals are attached."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
